      id: "lesson-7",
      title: "Managing the buyer pipeline",
      body: "## Purpose\n\nBuyer development is a continuous process. SMEs need a system for tracking opportunities, following up and understanding where commercial progress is occurring.\n\n## A. Buyer pipeline structure\n\nThe recommended pipeline stages are:\n\n1. Identified.\n2. Researched.\n3. Qualified.\n4. Contacted.\n5. Engaged.\n6. Requirements confirmed.\n7. Quotation submitted.\n8. Negotiation.\n9. Order confirmed.\n10. Closed - Won or Closed - Lost.\n\nThe platform should allow a learner to record the reason an opportunity moves between stages.\n\n## B. Buyer pipeline register\n\n| Field | Required information |\n| --- | --- |\n| Buyer ID | Unique reference |\n| Company name | Buyer identity |\n| Country | Buyer location |\n| Buyer category | Importer, distributor, retailer, institutional buyer, etc. |\n| Product | Product of interest |\n| Contact person | Relevant decision-maker |\n| Source | Where the buyer was identified |\n| Verification status | Not started, in progress, completed |\n| Pipeline stage | Current opportunity status |\n| Estimated opportunity value | Amount and currency, if known |\n| Last contact | Date |\n| Next action | Specific follow-up |\n| Responsible person | SME owner |\n| Next follow-up date | Planned date |\n| Outcome | Active, won, lost or on hold |\n\nEstimated opportunity value must not be reported as confirmed sales.\n\n## C. Follow-up discipline\n\nAfter contacting a buyer, the SME should:\n\n- Record the date and channel.\n- Record the buyer’s response.\n- Identify the next action.\n- Assign a responsible person.\n- Set a follow-up date.\n- Avoid sending repetitive or irrelevant messages.\n- Close inactive opportunities when appropriate.\n\n## D. Pipeline performance indicators\n\nSMEs can monitor:\n\n- Number of potential buyers identified.\n- Number researched.\n- Number qualified.\n- Number contacted.\n- Number of meaningful buyer responses.\n- Number of requirements received.\n- Number of quotations submitted.\n- Number of negotiations.\n- Number of confirmed orders.\n- Value of confirmed orders.\n- Reasons opportunities were lost.\n\nThese indicators help management identify where buyer conversion is breaking down.\n\n## Practical exercise\n\nLearners create a buyer pipeline containing at least five prospects and assign a next action to each.\n\n## Lesson output\n\nA Qualified Buyer Pipeline and Follow-up Register.",
