  staff: {
    facilitatorGuide: "## Facilitator prompts\n\n- Who actually buys your product?\n- Why would that buyer purchase from your business?\n- What evidence shows the buyer is relevant?\n- Who makes the purchasing decision?\n- What information does the buyer need before considering your offer?\n- What is the difference between an enquiry and a confirmed order?\n- What would make your quotation commercially unacceptable?\n- What should happen after the buyer receives the quotation?\n- How do you know which opportunities deserve more attention?\n\nThe facilitator should use the learners’ actual products and businesses where possible.\n\n## Assessor scoring guide\n\nLearners must demonstrate that they can move from buyer identification to a structured commercial opportunity.\n\nEach criterion is scored from 0 to 6.\n\n| Score | Performance description |\n| --- | --- |\n| 0 | No submission or no demonstrated capability |\n| 1 | Very limited understanding; major errors |\n| 2 | Partial capability; significant gaps |\n| 3 | Functional; basic requirements addressed |\n| 4 | Good; practical and mostly complete |\n| 5 | Strong; well-researched and commercially sound |\n| 6 | Excellent; clear, evidence-based and ready for implementation |\n\nThe assessor must record the reason for the failure and provide corrective feedback.\n\n## Case material notes\n\nWritten by the platform team, not Entrust. At a 25% margin the price is ETB 546,667 (USD 4,555.56, about USD 9.11 a jacket). A 10% discount gives ETB 492,000, with a gross profit of ETB 82,000 and a 16.67% margin, below the 18% minimum. The 15-day delivery is half the normal 30-day lead time. A learner should not accept either without changes.",
    liveSessionPlan: "Duration: 150 minutes\n\n| Time | Activity | Facilitator responsibility | Learner output |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 0–10 min | Introduction | Explain buyer development and conversion | Understanding of module |\n| 10–30 min | Buyer profiles and target markets | Help learners define their ideal buyers | Ideal Buyer Profile |\n| 30–50 min | Buyer identification and research | Demonstrate practical buyer research | Buyer Research Sheet |\n| 50–70 min | Verification and qualification | Challenge unsupported buyer claims | Buyer Qualification Assessment |\n| 70–80 min | Break |  |  |\n| 80–100 min | Buyer approach | Review introductions and product information | Buyer Introduction Package |\n| 100–120 min | Buyer meetings and requirements | Conduct simulated buyer discussions | Buyer Meeting Record |\n| 120–140 min | Quotations and negotiation | Review commercial offers and objections | Quotation and Negotiation Record |\n| 140–150 min | Pipeline management | Review follow-up and conversion practices | Qualified Buyer Pipeline |",
    hybridSequence: "The platform should contain seven lessons:\n\n| Lesson | Content | Required activity |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Understanding buyers and selecting target markets | Ideal Buyer Profile |\n| 2 | Finding and researching potential buyers | Buyer Research Sheet |\n| 3 | Buyer verification and qualification | Buyer Qualification Assessment |\n| 4 | Preparing a professional buyer approach | Buyer Introduction Package |\n| 5 | Managing buyer discussions and understanding requirements | Buyer Meeting Record |\n| 6 | Quotations, negotiation and conversion | Commercial Quotation and Negotiation Record |\n| 7 | Managing the buyer pipeline | Qualified Buyer Pipeline |\n\nEach lesson should include:\n\n- Instructional content.\n- A worked example.\n- A practical exercise.\n- A knowledge check.\n- A saved progress checkpoint.\n\nLearners should be able to complete the module independently and return to saved work.",
  },
